            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RiceMilkTaters"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Note, pie crust isn't in the ingredients, but I imagine a store bought one would be fine. I made my own personal recipe for pie crust. I'm giving it 4/5 stars for this reason, the taste is 5/5 stars. I wanted a recipe without a graham cracker crust, that was simple, and easy to convert to dairy-free for allergies. This was great. I used maple syrup instead of corn syrup and a little less sugar than needed because it was plenty sweet. I left out the caramel whipped cream topping and did a coconut cream reduction with coconut sugar instead. Turned out great--almost like a peanut butter cookie in pie form!",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-22T18:56:54.299Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great, easy peanut butter pie! I needed a recipe without cream cheese so I tried this. I wanted to make with ingredients on hand, so I substituted creamy peanut butter and 1/2 cup pure maple syrup for the dark corn syrup. Served warm with whipped cream and did not make the caramel sauce. Very good. I will try again with ingredients listed above to see the difference!",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-08T10:27:49.640Z"
          },
          {
